# gtk4 -- the toolkit every GNOME application is written in, and what
# gnome-shell's own UI is drawn with by way of libadwaita and St.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/gtk/4.18/gtk-4.18.5.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=bb5267a062f5936947d34c9999390a674b0b2b0d8aa3472fe0d05e2064955abc
SRC_DIR=gtk-4.18.5

# -Dx11-backend=true, AND THE CLAUSE IT REPLACES IS KEPT BECAUSE IT WAS NOT
# WRONG -- it was written before the thing that contradicts it existed.
#
# It read: "Wayland only, matching mesa: the X11 backend would need an X server
# to talk to, and there is none. An X application reaches this GTK through
# Xwayland when that is packaged, which does not require an X backend here."
#
# Every sentence of that is true OF APPLICATIONS, and the last one even
# anticipated Xwayland arriving. What it did not anticipate is a GTK 4 program
# whose whole job is to BE an X client:
#
#   mutter-x11-frames draws server-side decorations for X11 windows under
#   Xwayland. mutter builds it UNCONDITIONALLY whenever X11 client support is
#   on -- there is no frames option to turn off -- and it includes
#   gdk/x11/gdkx.h, which is this backend. So mutter cannot be built at all
#   with -Dxwayland=true against a GTK 4 that has no X11 backend.
#
# The distinction the old clause missed is between RUNNING an X server, which
# this tree still does not do, and being a CLIENT of one, which it now does the
# moment Xwayland is packaged. GTK's X11 backend is client-side code.
#
# THE COST, and it is a package deeper: this backend requires cairo-xlib, and
# cairo was disabled -Dxlib for the same reason by the same reasoning. That is
# corrected in pkgs/cairo/pkg.env, which carries the matching lineage note.
# Everything else it wants -- x11, xext, xrender, xi, xcursor, xdamage, xfixes,
# xrandr, xinerama, fontconfig -- is already packaged and already earlier in the
# build order. No new package anywhere in the cascade.
#
# WAYLAND REMAINS THE DEFAULT AND THE POLICY IS UNCHANGED. -Dwayland-backend
# stays true, broadway/win32/macos stay false, and GDK still prefers Wayland at
# runtime; GDK_BACKEND=x11 is what selects the other, and only an X client would
# ask.
#
# vulkan is disabled because the Vulkan loader is not packaged and mesa is built
# with no Vulkan drivers; GTK falls back to its GL renderer, which is what it
# used before 4.14 and what mesa provides.
#
# media-gstreamer is off until gstreamer is packaged. The visible cost is that
# GtkVideo cannot play anything -- no video thumbnails, no in-app playback.
# print-cups is off for the same reason: no CUPS, so no printing.
MESON_ARGS="-Dwayland-backend=true -Dx11-backend=true -Dbroadway-backend=false \
-Dwin32-backend=false -Dmacos-backend=false \
-Dvulkan=disabled -Dmedia-gstreamer=disabled -Dprint-cups=disabled \
-Dcloudproviders=disabled -Dsysprof=disabled -Dtracker=disabled -Dcolord=disabled \
-Dintrospection=enabled -Ddocumentation=false -Dman-pages=false \
-Dbuild-demos=false -Dbuild-examples=false -Dbuild-tests=false -Dbuild-testsuite=false"
